// The art kit: one style and one prop library for every scene file.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Before this file every scene drew its own props, and the same object came
// out differently each time it appeared:
//   - the observatory mountain was drawn three ways in three scenes, and its
//     trail broke into separate pieces that did not meet
//   - a treasure chest's lid and coins floated, because the lid was not hinged
//     to anything and the coins were drawn after the front face
//   - cafe cups and papers hovered above tabletops that had no real top
//     surface, and a cream tablecloth beside a lamp read as a second light
//   - the forest kept an older flat style while the cast moved to the croc look
//
// So the rules live here, once, and every prop obeys them by construction:
//
//   ONE LIGHT      from the upper left (tokens light.side). Lit faces left/up,
//                  one shade band on the right, one warm highlight. Never more.
//   INK OUTLINE    croc-style: the outline is the shape's own colour darkened
//                  toward brand ink, not one flat black. Width is per DEPTH
//                  layer and constant on screen whatever the prop's scale.
//   DEPTH          fg / mid / bg / far. Deeper layers veil toward the biome's
//                  haze colour and lose their outline. In dark interiors the
//                  haze is dark, so distance darkens (scene-art "inverts here").
//   CONTACT POINT  every prop is drawn in a LOCAL frame whose origin (0,0) is
//                  where it touches its surface: bottom centre. Place a prop by
//                  saying where its feet go, never where its box starts.
//   CONTACT SHADOW drawn by the prop itself, so it cannot be forgotten.
//   ANCHORS        bcArt.anchors(name, opts) returns named attach points in
//                  scene space: a table's 'top' surface, a chest's 'inside', a
//                  mountain's 'summit' and 'trailBase'. bcArt.on(anchor, ...)
//                  seats a child on that surface, so a cup cannot hover.
//   IDS            any gradient a prop defines is prefixed with opts.idp, so
//                  two scenes in one document never steal each other's fill.
//
// Public API (all on the one global, bcArt):
//   bcArt.prop(name, opts)        -> SVG <g> string
//   bcArt.anchors(name, opts)     -> { anchorName: {x,y} | {cx,cy,rx,ry} | ... }
//   bcArt.on(anchor, child, o)    -> child seated on a surface anchor
//   bcArt.sky(biome, idp)  bcArt.ground(biome, idp, horizonY)
//   bcArt.layer(depth, svg, biome) -> svg recoloured with that depth's haze
//   bcArt.shadow(x, y, width, depth)
//   bcArt.shade / light / ink / tone / haze / mix / palette
//   bcArt.PROPS (names), bcArt.VARIANTS (option sets the CI check renders)
//
// Common prop opts: x, y (scene position of the contact point), scale, flip,
// depth ('fg'|'mid'|'bg'|'far'), biome, idp, shadow:false, light:'left'|'right'.
//
